; walk-sex — the row delay repeats a row without re-reading it.
;
; Row 0 carries `S62` (frame delay 2), `SE1` (play the row twice), a note
; and a second `SEx` further right that loses — the LEFTMOST wins. Only
; the first play carries the frame delay and the note sounds once, so the
; row is one `(row …)` of fourteen ticks: one row READ.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
